I am a Contributer to BCLib (a utility library for BetterEnd and BetterNether) and we support ModMenu as it is an insanely helpful utility for players. However, we want to get rid of the dependency in our build environment. I did some testing and adding `ConfigScreenFactory` as well as `ModMenuApi` would allow us to have ModMenu integration without needing the build-dependency. Is it ok, if we include those files in our Repository. Currently I added the following comment to every file, but I am happy to change the wording: 

> // This File was included from TerraformersMC/ModMenu
// to enable a ModMenu-Integration without having to
// compile against the actual plugin in an attempt
// to reduce dependencies

Players will of course have to install ModMenu for this integration to work. It is just about our build system. Please let us know if you'd prefer that we not include those interfaces

I am using cloth config:
Some other mods suffer the same issue like for example OK Zoomer.

### The Problem

When I am opening the settings from outside modmenu there are no problems at all.

Now I integrate the Settings Screen Builder into modmenu and open it. I can set all values just fine..
But when I leave those settings and find myself back inside the modmenu GUI, then reopen it:

The "Save" Button is already activated, and I cant change the value back, because the save button gets deactivated when switching the toggles back.

==> **Modmenu is reusing the same Screen object while its GUI is opened, while Cloth Config [explicitly stated not to do that](https://shedaniel.gitbook.io/cloth-config/using-cloth-config/creating-a-config-screen):**.

I've found [the code where that is happening](https://github.com/TerraformersMC/ModMenu/blob/9f4e048ecd293648d5f7ead626eee5eaae40c10e/src/main/java/com/terraformersmc/modmenu/gui/ModsScreen.java#L133).

### All you need to do:

[ModsScreen.java](https://github.com/TerraformersMC/ModMenu/blob/9f4e048ecd293648d5f7ead626eee5eaae40c10e/src/main/java/com/terraformersmc/modmenu/gui/ModsScreen.java)

### **Add**
```
// As I've looked trough the code I've found out that it relies on the screen being constantly initialized ;-; so sad
// This is to Re-Initialize a Screen once it was already used; true if Screen was used once
private ImmutableMap<String, Boolean> configScreenUsages = new HashMap<>();

public Screen buildConfigScreen(String modid) {
	try {
		return configScreen = ModMenu.getConfigScreen(modid, this);
	} catch (Throwable e) {
		LOGGER.error("Error from mod '" + modid + "'", e);
		return null;
	}
}
```
### **Modify**
**Line 116**
```
for (Mod mod : ModMenu.MODS.values()) {
	configScreenCache.put(modId, getConfigScreen(mod.getId()));
	configScreenUsages.put(mod.getId(), false);
}
```
### **Modify**
**Line 129**
```
ButtonWidget configureButton = new ModMenuTexturedButtonWidget(width - 24, paneY, 20, 20, 0, 0, CONFIGURE_BUTTON_LOCATION, 32, 64, button -> {
	final String modid = Objects.requireNonNull(selected).getMod().getId();
	// <-=<-=-===-FROM HERE-===-=->=->
	
	// If it was used already, create new screen
	if (configScreenUsages.get(modid)) {
		configScreenCache.put(modId, getConfigScreen(modid));
	}
	
	//  <-=<-=-===-TO HERE-===-=->=->
	final Screen screen = configScreenCache.get(modid);
	if (screen != null) {
		client.openScreen(screen);
	} else {
		button.active = false;
	}
},
```

